@startuml MagicLinkSSO-Flow

title Magic Link SSO Authentication Flow (Magic Link + Optional Email OTP)

actor User
participant "Client App\n(Angular / Fastify /\nNext.js / Nuxt / Django)" as Client
participant "SSO Server" as SSO
participant "Email Server" as Email
collections "Grant + Token Services\n(verification JWT, OTP challenge,\naccess JWT, replay cache)" as GrantService

== Start Sign-In ==

User -> Client: Access Protected Page (/protected)
Client -> Client: Check auth cookie
alt Cookie exists and is valid
    Client -> User: Render protected content
else Cookie missing or invalid
    alt Hosted direct flow
        Client -> User: Redirect to SSO /signin\n?returnUrl=...&verifyUrl=...&scope=...
        User -> SSO: Open /signin and submit email
    else App-owned login flow
        Client -> User: Render local login UI
        User -> Client: Submit email address
        Client -> SSO: POST /signin\n{ email, returnUrl, verifyUrl, scope? }
    end
    SSO -> SSO: Resolve site from returnUrl/verifyUrl\nand authorize email + requested scope
    SSO -> GrantService: Create one-time grant\n(siteId + scope + jti + trusted URLs)
    opt Email OTP enabled
        SSO -> GrantService: Store HMAC-protected OTP challenge\nlinked to the same jti
    end
    SSO -> Email: Send magic link + optional OTP
    Email --> User: Deliver sign-in email

    == Complete One-Time Grant ==

    alt Magic link
        User -> Email: Click magic link
        Email -> User: Open trusted /verify-email?token=...
        alt App-owned callback
            User -> Client: GET /verify-email?token=...
            Client -> SSO: GET /verify-email?token=...\n(preview secret, JSON)
            SSO -> GrantService: Validate without consuming
            SSO --> Client: 200 JSON { email }
            Client -> User: Render no-store confirmation
            Client -> SSO: POST /verify-email { token }
        else Server-managed callback
            User -> SSO: GET /verify-email?token=...
            SSO -> GrantService: Validate without consuming
            SSO -> User: No-store confirmation;\nHttpOnly token + CSRF cookies
            User -> SSO: POST /verify-email (CSRF)
        end
        SSO -> GrantService: Validate and atomically consume jti
        SSO --> Client: Access token or trusted verification callback
    else Email OTP enabled
        alt App-owned code field
            User -> Client: Enter code in already-open app
            Client -> SSO: POST /verify-email/otp\n{ challengeId, code } (JSON)
        else Hosted code field
            User -> SSO: Enter code in already-open hosted page
            SSO -> SSO: POST /verify-email/otp (CSRF)
        end
        SSO -> GrantService: Verify code, expiry, and attempts
        alt Invalid code with attempts remaining
            SSO --> User: Generic error + same code-only form
        else Expired, exhausted, or consumed
            SSO --> User: Return to email form and start again
        else Valid code
            SSO -> GrantService: Atomically consume the same jti
            SSO --> Client: Access token or trusted verification callback
        end
    end

    opt Grant completed successfully
        Client -> Client: Verify expected issuer + audience\nand set HTTP-only auth cookie
        Client -> User: Redirect to protected page
    end
end

note over GrantService
The magic link and OTP are alternate exchanges for one grant.
Whichever succeeds first consumes its shared jti;
the other path cannot be replayed.
end note

@enduml
